# Normalize line endings in the repository: every text file is stored with LF
# in the index. Without this, core.autocrlf on Windows checkouts leaks CRLF into
# committed blobs, which makes `git diff --check` report phantom trailing
# whitespace and breaks shell scripts that must stay LF.
* text=auto

# Files that are executed as scripts must keep LF in the working tree too,
# otherwise bash rejects them on Windows (the pre-commit hook hit exactly this).
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Assets compiled into the binary with //go:embed must keep LF in the working
# tree. The embedded bytes are compared byte-for-byte against \n-based literals
# in Go source (and written back out verbatim when seeding a workspace), so a
# CRLF checkout on Windows makes those comparisons fail on every fresh clone.
# Every //go:embed root in the repository lives under internal/<pkg>/defaults/,
# except internal/web/dist, which is untracked build output.
internal/*/defaults/** text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF in the working tree.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch the bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zst binary
*.exe binary
